' v1.2's Settings page by keys (`OptionsSettingsPage`; `preset classic ai
' none seed 3 start 30 music remaster`). O, Tab, Down to Settings (past
' the Jukebox), Left into the page — on its first enabled line, the
' graphics (OptionsSettingsPage.cs:106-115; enabled since the look can be
' switched) — Down past Fullscreen (it can be switched under SDL's
' dummy driver), then Down twice to
' "Map Music NONE", Space: "Map Music KEEP" and its hint (`settings`); the
' choice is written to `user.txt` (a scripted run writes it where it runs,
' and no run reads it back).
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map (MapScene.cs:687-691)
mapclick 110,122
wait 60
press o
wait 5
press tab
press down               ' Jukebox
press down               ' Settings
press left               ' into the page: the graphics
press down               ' Fullscreen
press down               ' Music
press down               ' Map Music
press space              ' None -> Keep
wait 5
snap settings
press escape
wait 5
quit
